    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE THREE MUSKETEERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Three Musketeers is a film that grossed $27 million in North America and $7 million in other markets, totaling $34 million worldwide. It received poor reviews, with only 11% positive reviews on Rotten Tomatoes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Three Musketeers is a novel by Alexandre Dumas, known for its historical and dramatic narrative."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0206-a5486a961433</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROTTEN TOMATOES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rotten Tomatoes is a website that provides movie reviews and ratings, which gave The Three Musketeers 11% positive reviews."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0206-a5486a961433</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEPHEN HOLDEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stephen Holden is a film critic who reviewed The Three Musketeers, noting issues with the film's editing and d'Artagnan's appearance."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0206-a5486a961433</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE NEW YORK TIMES&quot;">
